<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 17-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 17-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Opal, with 60 mph winds, is in the eastern Philippine Sea near 16.5n/132.5e, moving north at 5 mph. Opal will intensify to a typhoon during th enext 12-18 hours, peaking with top winds near 90 mph in about 36 hours, before slow weakening begins. It remains a threat only to shipping at this time.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
